  "workflow": {
    "title": "vendor onboarding for a small manufacturing company",
    "summary": "A procurement employee submits a supplier request with a quotation, company details, and a proposed order value. An AI assistant reads the quotation and supplier record, compares the request with the approved supplier list, and prepares a recommendation. The procurement manager reviews the recommendation, and finance verifies bank details. Only an authorised procurement employee can add a vendor to the purchasing system. The assistant cannot change bank details, add a vendor, place an order, or send a payment. Requests with missing or conflicting records are paused for review. Rejection returns the request to the requester with an explanation; acceptance creates a reviewed onboarding record, not an order. The workflow uses a supplier register and a purchasing system, but exact products and API permissions are not yet defined. Operating countries, document retention periods, escalation deadlines, record ownership, and budget thresholds still need to be decided."
  },
